S137 LRC14 OPERATOR SEQUENCE TOURNAMENT
==============================================================================
[0] Assumption challenge / quotient declaration
  considered vertices:
    runners, gaps, Farey fractions, fraction payloads, C=27 shells,
    Kpq incidence owners, octahedral packet currents, Clebsch cuts,
    second-moment events, exact-period packets, and proof obligations.
  chosen vertices:
    operator/carrier roles, plus a C=27 shell quotient when the p=2
    branch is isolated.
  quotient preserves:
    exact Farey excess e=14p-q, binding denominator q, additive and
    product side channels, low-gap shell transfer, and state-lift fit.
  quotient destroys:
    exact time geometry and row-specific witnesses; those remain attached
    through M(S), q-threshold, and the C27 transfer label.
  challenged assumption:
    a single runner tournament or scalar payload is enough.  The live
    predicate needs a labelled operator packet before scalarization.

[1] Unit-excess Farey sequence fingerprints
  chain: p/q = p/(14p-1), so M-1/14 = 1/(14q)
       p/q     q   p+q    p*q         gap       Kpq q mod27 p*q mod27
      1/13    13    14     13       1/182      star      13        13
      2/27    27    29     54       1/378 two-block       0         0
      3/41    41    44    123       1/574  K33-wall      14        15
      4/55    55    59    220       1/770  K33-wall       1         4
      5/69    69    74    345       1/966  K33-wall      15        21
      6/83    83    89    498      1/1162  K33-wall       2        12
      7/97    97   104    679      1/1358  K33-wall      16         4
     8/111   111   119    888      1/1554  K33-wall       3        24
     9/125   125   134   1125      1/1750  K33-wall      17        18

  q      : detected polynomial degree 1; Delta=[14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14]; Delta2=[0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
  sum    : detected polynomial degree 1; Delta=[15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15]; Delta2=[0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
  product: detected polynomial degree 2; Delta=[41, 69, 97, 125, 153, 181]; Delta2=[28, 28, 28, 28, 28, 28]
  q^p and p^q are intentionally not polynomial lanes; they are
  magnitude-stress tests for quotients that forget scale.

  Readout:
    q      is the theorem-level binding scale: +14 on the chain.
    p+q    is the additive/Stern-Brocot lane: +15 on the chain.
    p*q    is the product/coimage area lane: quadratic, Delta2=28.
    q^p,p^q amplify magnitude and should not be used as denominators.

